  "body": "# Homarr v2 release flight check\n\nThis PR is the single release checklist. Add evidence beside each completed gate; validate one frozen candidate, and repeat affected checks when it changes.\n\n**Path:** finish fixes in `release/v2` \u2192 merge `release/v2` directly into `dev` \u2192 human-approved `dev \u2192 main` major release \u2192 verify public artifacts.\n\n## Current state \u00b7 2026-09-12\n\n- `release/v2`: `2049c6ade`; `dev`: `43a57a2d`; latest stable: **v1.77.1**.\n- [Previously validated baseline CI and preview publication](https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/actions/runs/34508074005), CodeQL and Workshop passed. This does **not** prove upgrade or browser behavior.\n- Release article #6790 and llama.cpp #6765 are merged. #6806 remains excluded. #6810 is closed and is not a release prerequisite; its earlier focused browser results do not establish acceptance of the final release candidate.\n- Direct merge path selected: `release/v2 \u2192 dev`. The branches currently have 65 dev-only / 606 v2-only commits. Their conflicts are resolved in #6821 (`0501c6f21`), which contains both current branch tips. Land that merge with dev ancestry preserved, then refresh the direct comparison. #6820 targets the old bottom stack and is not a prerequisite for this path.\n- #6824 is merged: source setup, production update docs, beta workflow and demo username protection. #6821 now merges current `dev` as well as `release/v2`; refreshed CI is pending. Next.js, Widgets and Translation typechecks and 37 focused tests passed. Dev fixes, translations and exact-build regression-report fields remain for review.\n- Check the [dev branch rules](https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/rules/687872) against the direct merge PR: the previous audit found a retired `Container and E2E` requirement. Reconcile required checks before landing. Rules on the old `v2` stack branch are not a prerequisite for this path.\n\n## Before release\n\n- [ ] **Integrate and freeze.** Review and land #6821 after CI with its merge ancestry preserved; exclude #6806. Prepare the direct `release/v2 \u2192 dev` merge, resolve conflicts, and verify preserved dev fixes. Land the reviewed result in `dev`; record candidate SHA and release owner. The individual stack layers do not need to land first.\n- [ ] **Pass release validation.** On that candidate, pass CI/CodeQL, docs/Workshop builds and both image architectures; reconcile required checks; attach a production dependency/image security report and resolve or explicitly accept release-critical findings.\n- [ ] **Record data-safety evidence.** Attach the completed v1 \u2192 v2 automatic migration checks and database coverage, including representative data and sign-in. Repeat affected cases only if migration changes land. Keep backup/restore and rollback evidence with the release record; users update their image normally.\n- [ ] **Check regressions against current dev.** Replay the same desktop/mobile flows and fixtures: login/permissions, boards and drag/resize, widget refresh/failure, integration setup, import/export and backup. Check v2-only Custom Widgets, Workshop, Assistant/MCP and onboarding separately. For each confirmed regression, link one issue with exact builds, reproduction steps, impact and an owner; check for duplicates and verify the same steps after a fix. Revisit open regressions and affected flows as release changes land.\n- [ ] **Prepare publication.** Verify production image/Workshop URLs and Helm guidance; coordinate the GA article with artifact availability (docs deploy from `dev`, and the article is already marked `draft: false`); prepare release notes, support and rollback ownership. Confirm Semantic Release selects v2.0.0 and keep the major-release human merge gate.\n\n## Release and follow-through\n\n- [ ] **Release, verify and announce.** Human-merge the approved `dev \u2192 main` PR; verify the v2.0.0 release, archives and immutable amd64/arm64 image digests. Smoke a public clean install and v1 upgrade; verify docs, Workshop and downloads; then announce and monitor upgrade/auth/data issues with a named rollback owner.\n\n**Candidate:** pending \u00b7 **Release / rollback owner:** pending \u00b7 **Evidence / accepted issues:** pending\n\n",
